---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maitri Shah | Work Experience"
  description="Research assistant and teaching assistant contributions in AI security and reliability."
>
  <header class="glass-card">
    <h1 class="hero-title">Work Experience</h1>
    <p class="hero-body">Core research and engineering contributions in Trustworthy AI.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-8 glass-card">
    <h2 class="section-title">Research Assistant | CISPA Helmholtz Center (SprintML Lab)</h2>

    <h3 class="project-title mt-5">Project: Watermark Radioactivity (NeurIPS 2026 Submission)</h3>
    <p class="copy">Investigating radioactive data: how watermark signals persist or decay when generative models are trained recursively on their own outputs.</p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">My Contributions</p>
    <ul class="list-clean">
      <li><strong>Technical Implementation:</strong> Integrated high-resolution generative backends, including <span class="metric">SANA 0.6B</span> and <span class="metric">Infinity-2B</span>, into a unified cross-architecture evaluation pipeline.</li>
      <li><strong>Manual Evaluation:</strong> Performed foundational manual assessments of Infinity-2B to establish radioactivity baselines before the automated pipeline was operational.</li>
      <li><strong>Statistical Innovation:</strong> Facilitated the transition from unstable P-values to <span class="metric">E-values</span>, providing non-asymptotic guarantees for black-box provenance detection.</li>
      <li><strong>Refactoring:</strong> Refactored detection implementations to resolve compatibility issues and improve stability across multi-GPU workflows.</li>
      <li><strong>Knowledge Base:</strong> Worked directly with StegaStamp, TrustMark, RivaGAN, and BitMark watermarking schemes during resilience testing.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Key Learning</p>
    <p class="copy">I learned how to manage distribution shifts in iterative training loops and why non-asymptotic metrics (E-values) are essential for reliable security claims in black-box scenarios.</p>

  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 glass-card">
    <h2 class="section-title">Teaching Assistant | Trustworthy Machine Learning (Saarland University / CISPA)</h2>
    <p class="copy"><strong>Scale:</strong> Supporting a graduate-level cohort of <span class="metric">100+ Master's students</span>.</p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">My Contributions</p>
    <ul class="list-clean">
      <li><strong>Co-leading Tutorials:</strong> Designed and conducted technical walkthroughs on assignment logic and adversarial attack methodology.</li>
      <li><strong>Managing GPU Cluster Setup:</strong> Managed cluster setup and SLURM troubleshooting for large-scale student assignments.</li>
      <li><strong>Co-developing Assignments:</strong> Contributed course materials and evaluation criteria for exams and practical projects.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Key Learning</p>
    <p class="copy">I developed the ability to translate complex research concepts into actionable engineering steps for others and learned to manage the technical infrastructure required for large-scale AI education.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 glass-card">
    <h2 class="section-title">Research Assistant (B.Tech) | QuadTransport</h2>
    <p class="copy"><strong>Optimization:</strong> Redesigned a Java-based Wasserstein distance computation using Quad-tree partitioning.</p>
    <p class="copy"><strong>Impact:</strong> Achieved <span class="metric">50x runtime reduction</span>, reducing execution from 35 minutes to 12 seconds.</p>
    <p class="copy"><strong>Key Learning:</strong> Deepened understanding of algorithmic efficiency and how spatial partitioning can reduce the complexity of high-dimensional distance calculations.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
